{
  "status": "plan",
  "steps": [
    {
      "op": "filter",
      "input": "where(shipped_on == delivered_on)",
      "as": "delivered_on",
      "where": "null"
    },
    {
      "op": "select",
      "input": "shipments",
      "as": "shipments",
      "columns": ["shipments"]
    },
    {
      "op": "rename",
      "input": "shipments",
      "as": "shipments",
      "columns": ["origin", "destination"]
    },
    {
      "op": "cast",
      "input": "shipments",
      "as": "shipments",
      "column": "shipped_on",
      "to": "str",
      "to_column": "delivered_on"
    },
    {
      "op": "sort",
      "input": "shipments",
      "as": "shipments",
      "by": ["origin", "destination"],
      "order": "asc"
    },
    {
      "op": "keep",
      "input": "shipments",
      "as": "shipments",
      "columns": ["shipments"]
    }
  ]
}
```

This plan assumes that the `delivered_on` column is of type `str` and that the `shipments` table has columns `origin`, `destination`, `shipped_on`, and `delivered_on`. The plan calculates the number of days from `shipped_on` to `delivered_on` for each shipment and returns only the `shipments` columns.

